  "name": "luh-multi-material-fused-filament-fabrication-cube-metal-filled-filaments",
  "notes": "This dataset consists of micro-computed tomography (µCT) images of a multi-material cube test specimen additively manufactured using fused filament fabrication (FFF) and metal-filled filaments. The cube is composed of eight smaller cubes, alternating the materials.\r\n\r\n* __Outer Dimensions:__ 20 x 20 x 20 mm³ (with each individual cube measuring 10 x 10 x 10 mm³)  \r\n* __Materials:__ colorFabb Steelfill and colorFabb Copperfill (PLA) \r\n* __FFF Machine:__ Flashforge Creator Pro 2 (refer to the included .gx file for printing parameters)  \r\n* __µCT Scanner:__ Bruker SkyScan 1275\r\n\r\n\r\n![Cube Section](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/453889ca-498f-40a8-8c5e-801fd6be16a4/resource/744f527c-6ec9-4fc2-a3f0-5dda4b8344e5/download/cube_section.png)\r\n\r\n![Cube Slice](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/453889ca-498f-40a8-8c5e-801fd6be16a4/resource/4f9d64c6-6092-4a0b-abaf-ca66b55add76/download/cube_slice.jpg)\r\n\r\nIn the reconstructed cross-sectional CT images, the darker material represents the denser copper-filled filament.\r\n\r\n### Acknowledgments\r\n\r\n* The project _“Computer tomograph for optomechatronic systems”_ was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) - Project number 432176896.",
